{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts","id":919301,"title":"Raising Auspice Renown and Shadow Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-22T13:45:05-07:00","id":919301,"title":"Raising Auspice Renown and Shadow Gifts","content":"When you raise Auspice Renown, do you also gain a free Shadow Gift Facet in that Renown in addition to another level in your Moon Gift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T13:47:36-07:00","id":919303,"title":"","content":"You do indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T13:51:45-07:00","id":919304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919303#post919303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure how you reached that conclusion when the book never actually says you get 'Both your auspice facet <b>and</b> a shadow facet' when you raise your Auspice renown.<br /> <br /> I'm even less sure how you reached this conclusion because that free Moon facet is generally far more powerful than any facet you're going to get from a shadow gift, so why are you getting two facets for the price of one renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T13:54:21-07:00","id":919305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919304#post919304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you reached that conclusion when the book never actually says you get 'Both your auspice facet <b>and</b> a shadow facet' when you raise your Auspice renown.<br /> <br /> I'm even less sure how you reached this conclusion because that free Moon facet is generally far more powerful than any facet you're going to get from a shadow gift, so why are you getting two facets for the price of one renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been confirmed by Stu since the Gifts mechanics were spoiled in open development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:03:07-07:00","id":919308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every time the Uratha gains a new dot of any Renown, she may unlock the respective Renown Facet in a Gift that she possesses at no cost. This spiritual development causes the Gift\u2019s marks to squirm and cut their way deeper into the Uratha\u2019s being, opening up the fresh Essence flows of the new Facets. </div> </div> </div>Even if 'Stu said it', I would like to at least hear why he said that. From my perspective I'm not seeing how that doesn't count when your moon gift automatically strengthens, My sister keeps telling me that Moon Gifts and Shadow Gifts are 'just different', the problem is that the differences feel hopelessly arbitrary to me, the <i>only</i> difference is that one is given by Luna, or Lunes, and the other is given by random spirits in the Hisil. Moon gifts are limited by your renown dots, sure, but they are all of them 'facets' when you get a new moon gift you do not get all of the facets up to your renown level, you have to purchase them with experiences,<br /> <br /> So how does it make any sense for you two be getting two facets when you raise that renown?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:26:11-07:00","id":919315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919304#post919304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you reached that conclusion when the book never actually says you get 'Both your auspice facet <b>and</b> a shadow facet' when you raise your Auspice renown.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gifts and Rites, p85</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Buying the first Facet of a Shadow Gift that your auspice or tribe has an affinity for (per their description in Chapter One) costs three Experiences. Buying the first Facet of any other Gift costs five Experiences. Having bought that first Facet, the character has unlocked the Gift, allowing the werewolf to buy additional Facets with Renown or Experiences. <b>A character learns a Facet of the appropriate Renown when she gains a dot in that Renown; this costs no Experiences.</b><br /> [\u2026]<br /> A werewolf always has one Moon Gift associated with her auspice. <b>She gains the appropriate Facet every time she gains a dot in her auspice Renown without spending any further Experiences.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>These are on the same page in neighboring paragraphs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Renown, p99</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As your character increases in Renown, she also increases her Gift dice pools and hunter\u2019s aspect rolls, and she also gains Facets of her Gifts. <b>Each time your character increases her auspice Renown, she unlocks a Facet of her Moon Gift. Every time she increases any Renown, she gains a Facet of a Shadow or Wolf Gift.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>These are on the same page in neighboring <i>sentences</i>. <br /> <br /> A Moon Gift makes you better at doing things appropriate to your auspice, but your auspice Renown is not only relevant to your auspice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-22-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:31:11-07:00","id":919317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts#post919301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you raise Auspice Renown, do you also gain a free Shadow Gift Facet in that Renown in addition to another level in your Moon Gift?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bAs the person who wrote the 2nd edition Gifts, I can confirm that yes, you get both Shadow and Moon Facets when raising Auspice Renown.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:40:23-07:00","id":919320,"title":"","content":"Simple deductive reasoning. Page 114 in the Forsaken 2e core states that &quot;Whenever the Uratha gains a dot in her Auspice Renown (including during character creation) she gains the Facet of equal dot rating to her new Renown total.&quot; The next couple of paragraphs go on to discrible Shadow Gifts. It is in this section it states that &quot;Every time the Uratha gains a new dot of <b>any*</b> Renown, she may unlock the respective Renown Facet in a Gift that she possesses at no cost.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, like I said, simple deductive reasoning. It's a matter of reading between the lines. I will admit though, it should be stated in a clearer fashion. But yeah, you do get a new Moon Facet and Shadow Facet when gaining a new level of Ausipce Renown.<br /> <br /> *emphisis mine.<br /> <br /> Edit: Poop! Satchel beat me to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T14:45:48-07:00","id":919324,"title":"","content":"Alright, so let's say you imported Purity Gifts from Signs of the Moon, and to further emphasize the hypothetical situation, let's say you also imported Warrior's Moon gifts from Lore of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Essentially when you raise your auspice renown, you get one free shadow facet, and then a facet from <b>one</b> of those auspice gift trees?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:34:39-07:00","id":919349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919324#post919324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, so let's say you imported Purity Gifts from Signs of the Moon, and to further emphasize the hypothetical situation, let's say you also imported Warrior's Moon gifts from Lore of the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Essentially when you raise your auspice renown, you get one free shadow facet, and then a facet from <b>one</b> of those auspice gift trees?</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the many differences between Moon Gifts and Shadow Gifts is that Moon Gifts have to be learned in ascending order.<br /> <br /> So if you raised your Purity from 1-3 while gaining Purity Gifts, and earned a fourth dot of Purity Renown, you could only have it in Warrior's Moon if you had already purchased the first three gifts in line. Otherwise Purity is the only Moon Gift line you have a fourth dot ready for.<br /> <br /> If you had 1-3 in Purity and Warrior's Moon you could choose which to get the free Moon Gift in, then purchase the other.<br /> <br /> 'Opening' a Moon Gift costs 5 Experience, including the cost of the first Gift. Each additional Moon Gift afterwards in the line costs 2, and you can never have higher than the corresponding Auspice.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Yes, you get one Shadow Gift and one Moon Gift of the appropriate dot for that Auspice. P114, 'Whenever the Uratha gains a dot in her auspice Renown...she gains the Facet <i>of equal dot rating</i> to her new Renown total.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-22-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T01:32:35-07:00","id":919590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919308#post919308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if 'Stu said it', I would like to at least hear why he said that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whether you like it or not, it's the way it officially works. Feel free to change it for your game, but for the OP, your understanding is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T16:13:03-07:00","id":920615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919308#post919308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if 'Stu said it', I would like to at least hear why he said that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh... Cause that's how it works?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919308#post919308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my perspective I'm not seeing how that doesn't count when your moon gift automatically strengthens, My sister keeps telling me that Moon Gifts and Shadow Gifts are 'just different', the problem is that the differences feel hopelessly arbitrary to me, ]the <i>only</i> difference is that one is given by Luna, or Lunes, and the other is given by random spirits in the Hisil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your sister is right.<br /> <br /> You're really downplaying the fact that they're given by spirits native to a place so different from Earth the freaking Idigam were banished there because the local shadow was too alien to sustain them. It's also not the only difference, because Moon Gifts are directly tied to Auspice, which Shadow Gifts are not, and they're an inherent part of a werewolf's nature as descendants of Luna, which Shadow Gifts are not. And, even setting all of that aside, who cares if it's arbitrary or not? Big deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/919301-raising-auspice-renown-and-shadow-gifts?p=919308#post919308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moon gifts are limited by your renown dots, sure, but they are all of them 'facets' when you get a new moon gift you do not get all of the facets up to your renown level, you have to purchase them with experiences,<br /> <br /> So how does it make any sense for you two be getting two facets when you raise that renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that's how Moon Gifts work. Moon Gifts are not the same thing as Shadow Gifts, mechanically or narratively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-24-2016, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}